  "note": "Annual election of one-third of the Ballyclare Urban Council, January 1931. Two nominations were received for three vacancies (Belfast News-Letter, 6 January 1931, p. 9). The third retiring member, Mr. Samuel Coleman, J.P., did not seek re-election; one seat was therefore left to be filled. Returned unopposed."
